Reason: removes ff_h264_decoder and ff_aac_decoder from the Chrome-branded
FFmpeg configuration for macOS arm64; companion to
third_party-ffmpeg-BUILD.gn.patch, which drops their sources.
Licence: this patch modifies FFmpeg's generated configuration, which is
LGPL-2.1-or-later. The modified FFmpeg (libffmpeg.dylib, built as its own
library with is_component_ffmpeg) must be offered in source form under the
LGPL, as plan.md §3.7 notes. Add the other OS/CPU configurations when those
ports start.
No upstream bug.
Repo: third_party/ffmpeg

diff --git a/chromium/config/Chrome/mac/arm64/libavcodec/codec_list.c b/chromium/config/Chrome/mac/arm64/libavcodec/codec_list.c
index fe5adb0..7d9debf 100644
--- a/chromium/config/Chrome/mac/arm64/libavcodec/codec_list.c
+++ b/chromium/config/Chrome/mac/arm64/libavcodec/codec_list.c
@@ -1,6 +1,4 @@
 static const FFCodec * const codec_list[] = {
-    &ff_h264_decoder,
-    &ff_aac_decoder,
     &ff_flac_decoder,
     &ff_mp3_decoder,
     &ff_vorbis_decoder,
